- `action(n9, ...)`, `action(n10, ...)`, `action(n11, ...)`, `end(e1)`, `end(e2)`, `end(e3)`: The source describes a single repetition phase and a single termination point ("Repeat the same steps if necessary. The process concludes once all steps have been completed."). The model hallucinates three duplicate repeat actions, three disjoint branches, and three independent end nodes, fragmenting the intended unified progression.
